  "caveats": [
    "lambda is a linear (Kyle-form) impact coefficient. Real impact is closer to a square root in trade size; linear is what closes the fixed point in a form that can be solved, and it overstates amplification at large K.",
    "kappa and Theta are free O(1) parameters, swept rather than fitted. Levels of K_nash and K_star inherit that freedom; the Nash-above-social wedge does not, since it follows from m'(K) > 0 for any admissible parameters.",
    "No crowding observation of any kind enters this file. K_star here is a prediction to be compared against realised crowding in crowding_test.py, not a fit to it."
